"a231093633ea0257b5f8f059c3776c4704c402a7","mtime":"1547527904","size":"38961","md5":"91e912e01e3c57f88c564fc61160a902","crc32":"28958055","sha1":"2516e6b97a5de80409fb5b04c0fe3a7b6bd64ef9","format":"Archive BitTorrent"},{"name":"london_airport_TNA_files.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","md5":"daa6102783afc05802f50af937b1f14b","summation":"md5"},{"name":"london_airport_TNA_meta.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","mtime":"1547527897","size":"1550","md5":"23b36f714a92733ac0f6a36eebf6c960","crc32":"360bef87","sha1":"d4aa26766d9cc3dffae7e16ba9945b36625d0faa"},{"name":"london_airport_TNA_reviews.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","mtime":"1202603610","size":"1572","md5":"ae8d8ae8c2aafcda726881c669ec03a5","crc32":"a58022d3","sha1":"70ef7c8970abf41e365acc2f08eca136598d7f44"},{"name":"london_airport_TNA_tags.xml","source":"original","format":"Metadata","md5":"f3664929813efa2000ef468888712c26","mtime":"1140435541","size":"90","crc32":"dd39048d","sha1":"c05b223f6207561ebff1b61da624360242d5ee75"}],"files_count":78,"item_last_updated":1694226646,"item_size":920608007,"metadata":{"identifier":"london_airport_TNA","title":"London Airport","mediatype":"movies","collection":["british_gov_public_films","ephemera"],"subject":"Heathrow; ariport; London","description":"The story of a great engineering feat - the building, at Heathrow, of one of the largest airports in the world.April 1944 Great Western Aerodrome started its transformation from a privately owned small grass airfield to Heathrow. One of the worlds busiest airports. Londons main civil airport replacing Croydon Airport.\n\nThe airport opened fully for civilian use on 31 May 1946. London Heathrow International Airport's one terminal was in fact an army surplus tent situated a short walk from the aircraft.","date":"1949","hidden":"true","publicdate":"2005-10-10 00:25:10","addeddate":"2005-10-10 07:25:04","uploader":"florian@archive.org","sponsor":"Central Office of Information for Ministry of Civil Aviation","publisher":"Crown Film Unit","sound":"sound","color":"color","runtime":"9:29","credits":"Public Information Films","rights":"UK Crown Copyright","language":"english","coverage":"Great Britain","updatedate":"2005-10-10 00:27:22","updater":"nVIR","backup_location":"ia903600_10","ia_orig__runtime":"9 Minutes 29 Seconds"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"Having been through Heathrow numerous times, it was odd to see how it looked a few decades ago: about the only similarity is the runway arrangement (and the runways back then looked pretty scary compared to the ones they have today!). I never realised it was built on farmland, today it's so built-up that it's hard to imagine being any different.","reviewtitle":"Looked different in those days","stars":"3","reviewer":"movieman","createdate":"2005-11-27 14:58:25","reviewdate":"2005-11-27 14:58:25"},{"reviewbody":"Slightly strange overview of Heathrow (which was the name of the land used by Villagers), which was then called London Airport and all it's services. We learn that the airport transport \"Men And Cargo\" which is a pretty harsh term to use for women if you ask me. Anyways, the building of this airport is shown.. I'm pretty sure a lot of it is stock footage which had nothing to do with the airport, but never mind that. Soon, the airport which was going to be used \"to finish off the Japs!\" is finished! Huzzah!","reviewtitle":"LONDON AIRPORT IS ON THE MAP!","reviewer":"Spuzz","reviewdate":"2008-02-10 00:33:30","createdate":"2008-02-10 00:33:30","stars":"3"}],"server":"dn800302.us.archive.org","simplelists":{"solo_manifest":{"solo_manifest_dn800302":{"sys_changed_by":{"source":"task","task_id":"5408040611"},"sys_last_changed":"2026-06-01 08:27:41.282244"}}},"solo":true,"uniq":818796125,"workable_servers":["dn800302.us.archive.org"]}